        {
          "id": "tts-24-9101",
          "type": "tts",
          "title": "Lecture 1",
          "text": "The Carter family always enjoys the weekend! Beth plays football for herschool. She always has a match on Saturday morning. She’s the goalkeeper,so she usually comes home with mud everywhere! Danny plays footballfor his school team, too, and always plays on Saturday afternoons. Theyusually ride their bikes to the football matches. Sometimes, when it rains,Mr Carter takes them in the car. Danny and Beth always leave their dirty football kit on thefloor in the kitchen. They never put it in the washing machine!Mrs Carter is a very good artist. She draws pictures of the pets. She oftendraws funny cartoons to make Danny and Beth laugh. When she draws,Mrs Carter listens to podcasts about sport and travel. On Sundays Mr Carterusually washes the car. He never listens to podcasts. Sometimes he goesfishing with Sam, his next-door neighbour. They are good friends. Whenthey catch fish they never keep them. They always put them back in theriver. For them it is only a sport and a time to chat.When there is music in the house, Eric and Ernie always dance. Theysometimes sing, too. CAW! CAW! Alfie usually chases Sybil around thehouse, and Sybil always escapes!",
